+1. **Primary Swine Macrophage Cultures**: Prepare primary macrophage cultures from heparin-swine blood by incubating at 37 °C for 1–2 hours for erythrocyte sedimentation. Separate mononuclear leukocytes using a Ficoll-Paque density gradient (specific gravity 1.079). Culture the monocyte/macrophage fraction in plastic Primaria tissue culture flasks using macrophage-culturing media (RPMI 1640 supplemented with 30% L929 supernatant, 20% heat-inactivated gamma-irradiated FBS, 1X antibiotics/antimycotics, 1X gentamicin, and 30% complementary plasma) for 24 hours at 37 °C under 5% CO2. Detach adherent cells using 10 µM EDTA in DPBS (incubate at 37 °C for 20 min), wash twice with macrophage wash medium (RPMI 1640, 1X antibiotics/antimycotics, 1X gentamicin), and re-seed into Primaria plates or cryopreserve.
 
